      "sourceTextSha256": "f7bc6c5edbe3d8ed3c250c714a9d38964b5df1a63804fd81fa3b59c4ccb948fb",
      "text": "Day 4 · Breakfast, then a 4-hour excursion to Corcovado: an open train climbs through the Tijuca Forest to the statue of Christ the Redeemer (38 m), at about 710 m, inaugurated in 1931, with a breathtaking panorama of the Rio–Niterói Bridge, Guanabara Bay, the Botanical Garden, the Maracanã Stadium and Sugar Loaf. We recommend watching the sunset from the rocks of Arpoador, and seafood at the Marius restaurant in the evening (around USD 130 per person).",
